Keep a `receive_messages` turn open until the work it started has finished. The
result that answers the caller arrives while a backgrounded delegation is still
running, and ending the turn there closed the subagent's parent out from under
it: the Task tool was failed as never having returned, and the subagent — its
launch block already discarded — reappeared under the next turn's agent span
under a placeholder name. A task still running when the stream ends is no
longer reported as an error either, and a message naming a subagent whose span
has already ended no longer re-opens the subtree.
